  "english": [
    "<b>And if it is not defined by its boundaries, up to how much</b> of the field is acquired by one strike of the hoe? <b>Rav Pappa said:</b> He acquires as far <b>as an ox driver goes and returns,</b> i.e., the size of a standard furrow, beginning where the hoe entered the ground.",
    "§ <b>Rav Yehuda says</b> that <b>Shmuel says:</b> With regard to the <b>property of a gentile</b> that was sold to a Jew for money, <b>it is</b> ownerless <b>like a desert</b> until the purchaser performs an act of acquisition; <b>anyone who takes possession of it</b> in the interim has <b>acquired it. What is the reason</b> for this? The <b>gentile relinquishes</b> ownership of it <b>from</b> the moment <b>when</b> the <b>money reaches his hand,</b> while the <b>Jew</b> who purchased it <b>does not acquire</b> it <b>until the deed reaches his hand. Therefore,</b> in the period of time between the giving of the money and the receiving of the deed, the property <b>is like a desert, and anyone who takes possession of it</b> has <b>acquired it.</b>",
    "<b>Abaye said to Rav Yosef: Did Shmuel</b> actually <b>say this? But doesn’t Shmuel say</b> that <b>the law of the kingdom is the law,</b> i.e., the <i>halakha</i> obligates Jews to observe the laws of the locale in which they reside, <b>and the king said</b> that <b>land may not be acquired without a document?</b> Therefore, taking possession should not be effective for acquisition. Rav Yosef <b>said to him: I do not know</b> how to reconcile this contradiction, but <b>there was an incident in</b> the village of <b>Dura that</b> was founded by <b>shepherds, where</b> there was <b>a Jew who purchased land from a gentile</b> by giving money, <b>and</b> in the interim <b>another Jew came</b> and <b>plowed it a bit.</b> The two Jews <b>came before Rav Yehuda</b> for a ruling, and he <b>established</b> the property <b>in the possession of the second</b> individual. This accords with the ruling of Shmuel that the property is ownerless until a Jew performs an act of acquisition.",
    "Abaye <b>said to him: Are you saying</b> that the incident occurred in <b>Dura that</b> was founded by <b>shepherds?</b> Proof cannot be brought from that case, as <b>there</b> the <b>fields were concealed, since</b> the owners of fields <b>would not pay the land tax [<i>taska</i>] to the king, and the king says</b> that <b>one who pays land tax</b> may <b>profit</b> from <b>the field.</b> Therefore, in that case, the gentile who sold the property did not actually own it, and consequently by the laws of the kingdom could not sell it. The one who took possession of the property acquired it in accordance with the law of the kingdom, as he committed to pay the land tax. Elsewhere, one would not acquire the field until he received a deed of sale from the gentile.",
    "The Gemara relates: <b>Rav Huna purchased land from a gentile. Another Jew came and plowed it slightly.</b> Rav Huna and that Jew <b>came before Rav Naḥman,</b> who <b>established</b> the property <b>in the possession</b> of the latter. Rav Huna <b>said to</b> Rav Naḥman: <b>What are you thinking</b> in issuing this ruling? Is it <b>because Shmuel says</b> that <b>the property of a gentile is like a desert, and anyone who takes possession of it</b> has <b>acquired it?</b>"
  ],
  "gemara": [
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "<span class=\"sentence\" id=\"0\" type=\"start\">&star;</span>וְשֶׁאֵינָהּ מְסוּיֶּימֶת בִּמְצָרֶיהָ, עַד כַּמָּה? אָמַר <span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-amora\" data-sage-type=\"amora\" title=\"Rav Pappa, fifth-generation Amora\" data-authority-id=\"2518\" data-full-name=\"Rav Pappa\" data-name-he=\"רב פפא\" data-crossline-group=\"name-ref-crossline-4896\">רַב</span>",
      "segment_ids": [
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "<span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-amora\" data-sage-type=\"amora\" title=\"Rav Pappa, fifth-generation Amora\" data-authority-id=\"2518\" data-full-name=\"Rav Pappa\" data-name-he=\"רב פפא\" data-crossline-group=\"name-ref-crossline-4896\">פָּפָּא</span>: <span class=\"ein_mishpat_marker\" data-ein-mishpat-id=\"0\" data-marker-letter=\"א\">א</span>כִּדְאָזֵיל תַּיָּירָא דְשׁוֹרֵי וְהָדַר. <span class=\"sugya-marker sugya-marker-steinsaltz\" data-sugya-kind=\"steinsaltz\" data-sugya-id=\"168\" data-sentence-id=\"1\" data-steinsaltz-label=\"א\"></span> <span class=\"sentence\" id=\"1\" type=\"start\">&star;</span>אָמַר <span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-amora\" data-sage-type=\"amora\" title=\"Rav Yehuda bar Yeḥezkel, second-generation Amora\" data-authority-id=\"1394\" data-full-name=\"Rav Yehuda bar Yeḥezkel\" data-name-he=\"רב יהודה בר יחזקאל\" data-crossline-group=\"name-ref-crossline-4897\">רַב</span>",
      "segment_ids": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "<span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-amora\" data-sage-type=\"amora\" title=\"Rav Yehuda bar Yeḥezkel, second-generation Amora\" data-authority-id=\"1394\" data-full-name=\"Rav Yehuda bar Yeḥezkel\" data-name-he=\"רב יהודה בר יחזקאל\" data-crossline-group=\"name-ref-crossline-4897\">יְהוּדָה</span> אָמַר <span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-amora\" data-sage-type=\"amora\" title=\"Shmuel II, first-generation Amora\" data-authority-id=\"2763\" data-full-name=\"Shmuel II\" data-name-he=\"שמואל\">שְׁמוּאֵל</span><span class=\"ein_mishpat_marker\" data-ein-mishpat-id=\"1\" data-marker-letter=\"ב\">ב</span>: נִכְסֵי גּוֹי הֲרֵי הֵן",
      "segment_ids": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "כְּמִדְבָּר, כׇּל הַמַּחְזִיק בָּהֶן זָכָה בָּהֶן. מַאי טַעְמָא? גּוֹי –",
      "segment_ids": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "מִכִּי מָטוּ זוּזֵי לִידֵיהּ אִסְתַּלַּק לֵיהּ, יִשְׂרָאֵל",
      "segment_ids": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "לָא קָנֵי עַד <span class=\"ein_mishpat_marker\" data-ein-mishpat-id=\"2\" data-marker-letter=\"ג\">ג</span>דְּמָטֵי שְׁטָרָא לִידֵיהּ. הִלְכָּךְ הֲרֵי הֵן",
      "segment_ids": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "כְּמִדְבָּר, וְכׇל הַמַּחְזִיק בָּהֶן זָכָה בָּהֶן. <span class=\"sentence\" id=\"2\" type=\"start\">&star;</span>אֲמַר לֵיהּ <span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-amora\" data-sage-type=\"amora\" title=\"Abaye, fourth-generation Amora\" data-authority-id=\"121\" data-full-name=\"Abaye\" data-name-he=\"אביי\">אַבָּיֵי</span>",
      "segment_ids": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "<span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-amora\" data-sage-type=\"amora\" title=\"Rav Yosef I, third-generation Amora\" data-authority-id=\"1764\" data-full-name=\"Rav Yosef I\" data-name-he=\"רב יוסף בר חייא\">לְרַב יוֹסֵף</span>: מִי אָמַר <span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-amora\" data-sage-type=\"amora\" title=\"Shmuel II, first-generation Amora\" data-authority-id=\"2763\" data-full-name=\"Shmuel II\" data-name-he=\"שמואל\">שְׁמוּאֵל</span> הָכִי?! וְהָאָמַר",
      "segment_ids": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "<span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-amora\" data-sage-type=\"amora\" title=\"Shmuel II, first-generation Amora\" data-authority-id=\"2763\" data-full-name=\"Shmuel II\" data-name-he=\"שמואל\">שְׁמוּאֵל</span>: <span class=\"ein_mishpat_marker\" data-ein-mishpat-id=\"3\" data-marker-letter=\"ד\">ד</span>דִּינָא דְמַלְכוּתָא דִּינָא; וּמַלְכָּא אָמַר: לָא",
      "segment_ids": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "לִיקְנֵי אַרְעָא אֶלָּא בְּאִיגַּרְתָּא! אֲמַר לֵיהּ: אֲנָא לָא",
      "segment_ids": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "יָדַעְנָא; עוֹבָדָא הֲוָה בְּדוּרָא דְרָעֲוָתָא, בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל",
      "segment_ids": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "דִּזְבַן אַרְעָא מִגּוֹי, וַאֲתָא יִשְׂרָאֵל אַחֲרִינָא",
      "segment_ids": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "רָפֵיק בָּהּ פּוּרְתָּא; אֲתָא לְקַמֵּיהּ <span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-amora\" data-sage-type=\"amora\" title=\"Rav Yehuda bar Yeḥezkel, second-generation Amora\" data-authority-id=\"1394\" data-full-name=\"Rav Yehuda bar Yeḥezkel\" data-name-he=\"רב יהודה בר יחזקאל\">דְּרַב יְהוּדָה</span>,",
      "segment_ids": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "אוֹקְמַהּ בִּידָא דְּשֵׁנִי. <span class=\"sentence\" id=\"3\" type=\"start\">&star;</span>אֲמַר לֵיהּ: דּוּרָא דְרָעֲוָתָא קָאָמְרַתְּ?!",
      "segment_ids": [
        3
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "הָתָם בָּאגֵי מִטַּמְּרִי הֲווֹ – דְּאִינְהוּ גּוּפַיְיהוּ לָא הֲווֹ",
      "segment_ids": [
        3
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "יָהֲבִי טַסְקָא לְמַלְכָּא, וּמַלְכָּא אֲמַר: מַאן דְּיָהֵיב",
      "segment_ids": [
        3
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "טַסְקָא, לֵיכוֹל אַרְעָא. <span class=\"sentence\" id=\"4\" type=\"start\">&star;</span><span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-amora\" data-sage-type=\"amora\" title=\"Rav Huna (רב הונא) — second/third-generation Amora, principal disciple of Rav and head of Sura\" data-authority-id=\"895\" data-full-name=\"Rav Huna\" data-name-he=\"רַב הוּנָא א׳\" data-resolution-rule=\"rav_huna_setam_default\" data-resolution-explanation=\"Identified as Rav Huna of Sura (895) on the setam principle: Rashi (Yevamot 83b) and Hyman rule that a plain, unqualified «רב הונא» is certainly this Rav Huna.\" data-resolution-reasons=\"[{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;scholarly_source&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Setam-Rav-Huna principle&quot;,&quot;detail&quot;:&quot;Rashi (Yevamot 83b) and Hyman rule that a plain, unqualified «רב הונא» is certainly the famous Rav Huna of Sura — «אבל היכי דאתמר סתמא ודאי הוא ר\\&quot;ה». No later or patronymic qualifier is present here.&quot;,&quot;attribution&quot;:&quot;Rashi, Yevamot 83b s.v. אמרי בי רב (with Hyman, s.v. רב הונא)&quot;}]\">רַב הוּנָא</span> זְבֵן אַרְעָא",
      "segment_ids": [
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "מִגּוֹי, אֲתָא יִשְׂרָאֵל אַחֵר רָפֵיק בַּהּ פּוּרְתָּא.",
      "segment_ids": [
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "אֲתָא לְקַמֵּיהּ <span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-amora\" data-sage-type=\"amora\" title=\"Rav Naḥman bar Ya’akov, third-generation Amora\" data-authority-id=\"2285\" data-full-name=\"Rav Naḥman bar Ya’akov\" data-name-he=\"רב נחמן בר יעקב\">דְּרַב נַחְמָן</span>, אוֹקְמַהּ בִּידֵיהּ. אֲמַר לֵיהּ:",
      "segment_ids": [
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "מַאי דַּעְתָּיךְ? דְּאָמַר <span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-amora\" data-sage-type=\"amora\" title=\"Shmuel II, first-generation Amora\" data-authority-id=\"2763\" data-full-name=\"Shmuel II\" data-name-he=\"שמואל\">שְׁמוּאֵל</span>: נִכְסֵי גּוֹי",
      "segment_ids": [
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "275px",
      "width": "380px",
      "text": "הֲרֵי הֵן כְּמִדְבָּר, וְכׇל הַמַּחְזִיק בָּהֶם זָכָה?",
      "segment_ids": [
        4
      ]
    }
  ],
